.th RMTREE VIII 11/4/78
.sh NAME
rmtree \*- remove a directory tree
.sh SYNOPSIS
.bd /etc/rmtree
name [ initial directory ]
.sh DESCRIPTION
.it Rmtree
removes an entire directory tree starting with
.it name
which is usually a directory name.
The default
.it "initial directory"
is
.it /tmp.
Circularly linked directories are no problem,
but mounted file systems are left alone.
Any problems encountered cause termination of ancestor directory
removal,
with the mode of the offending file changed to 0,
and its owner changed to root.
.sh "SEE ALSO"
init(VIII)
.sh DIAGNOSTICS
yes
.sh AUTHOR
Piers Lauder (\ University of Sydney\ )
